    fix(bench): C365 — the cancel-path tests fire their stop at the moment they test, not mid-grade (S27-P3)
    
    test_c147_cancel's SIGTERM test now waits for the client to linger AND the step-1 snapshot grade to return; the fake contract
    client writes its cancel file after step 1 is recorded, just before the sleep its comment names. Both raced a slow process
    launch (an endpoint agent checks every exec): the abort killed an in-flight grader (TransportAbort masked exit 143), or the
    cancel landed before any assistant message (empty export). Test-only; the runner's abort-vs-grade race is a recorded residual
    (C365), fixed at the next probe identity rotation. 75 / 75 three runs. Records C364 / C365.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

